{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"USN-9138-1","published":"2026-11-17T17:06:33Z","modified":"2026-11-18T14:28:20.001126931Z","related":["UBUNTU-CVE-2020-5395","UBUNTU-CVE-2020-5496"],"upstream":["CVE-2020-5395","CVE-2020-5496","UBUNTU-CVE-2020-5395","UBUNTU-CVE-2020-5496"],"summary":"fontforge vulnerabilities","details":"It was discovered that FontForge incorrectly handled memory when reading\nSFD files, leading to a use-after-free. If a user or automated system were\ntricked into opening a specially crafted SFD file, an attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause FontForge to crash, resulting in a denial\nof service, or possibly execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2020-5395)\n\nIt was discovered that FontForge incorrectly handled certain SFD files,\nleading to a heap-based buffer overflow. If a user or automated system were\ntricked into opening a specially crafted SFD file, an attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause FontForge to crash, resulting in a denial\nof service, or possibly execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2020-5496)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"fontforge","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:16.04:LTS","purl":"pkg:deb/ubuntu/fontforge?arch=source&distro=esm-apps-legacy%2Fxenial"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"20120731.b-7.1ubuntu0.1+esm2"}]}],"versions":["20120731.b-5","20120731.b-5ubuntu1","20120731.b-7.1","20120731.b-7.1ubuntu0.1","20120731.b-7.1ubuntu0.1+esm1"],"ecosystem_specific":{"availability":"Available with Ubuntu Pro with Legacy support add-on: https://ubuntu.com/pro","binaries":[{"binary_name":"fontforge","binary_version":"20120731.b-7.1ubuntu0.1+esm2"},{"binary_name":"fontforge-common","binary_version":"20120731.b-7.1ubuntu0.1+esm2"},{"binary_name":"fontforge-nox","binary_version":"20120731.b-7.1ubuntu0.1+esm2"},{"binary_name":"libfontforge1","binary_version":"20120731.b-7.1ubuntu0.1+esm2"},{"binary_name":"libgdraw4","binary_version":"20120731.b-7.1ubuntu0.1+esm2"},{"binary_name":"python-fontforge","binary_versio